WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.778
[MUSIC]

00:00:10.778 --> 00:00:13.149
I come from a real simple background.

00:00:13.149 --> 00:00:15.860
My mom cleaned houses,
my dad was a Navy mechanic.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:18.047
They both immigrated from Mexico.

00:00:18.047 --> 00:00:20.282
I'm the first of my family
to graduate from College.

00:00:20.282 --> 00:00:24.990
Just considering where I come from and
where I'm at today, every day that I

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:29.264
wake up and get to do something here
in this space is like a blessing.

00:00:29.264 --> 00:00:32.181
So I don't take it for
granted, and just looking for

00:00:32.181 --> 00:00:36.175
something more in the day to day,
more than just a business challenge.

00:00:36.175 --> 00:00:38.976
I'm Arnulfo Ventura,
I'm the CEO of Beanfields.

00:00:38.976 --> 00:00:43.761
I've been in the food and beverage
industry for the last 12 years, and

00:00:43.761 --> 00:00:45.336
GSB class of 2008.

00:00:45.336 --> 00:00:49.969
What I learned the most from the GSB
that still serves me well today,

00:00:49.969 --> 00:00:54.929
it's that it's the answer to that
question that everybody has to answer

00:00:54.929 --> 00:00:59.722
to in the process of applying to the GSB,
is what matters to you most and

00:00:59.722 --> 00:01:02.186
why, and not losing sight of that.

00:01:02.186 --> 00:01:07.890
[MUSIC]

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:11.480
Beanfields is a company
that started in 2010, and

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:15.459
it was ultimately founded with
the idea of making a better for

00:01:15.459 --> 00:01:19.767
you tortilla chip, a chance to
provide an alternative for corn.

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:24.335
And so our products are made
from a composition of navy bean,

00:01:24.335 --> 00:01:26.404
black bean and brown rice.

00:01:26.404 --> 00:01:29.585
Think of a Doritos, but perhaps healthier.

00:01:29.585 --> 00:01:33.422
Still a small company in the neighbourhood
of around 16 direct employees,

00:01:33.422 --> 00:01:35.499
a larger extended force in the hundreds.

00:01:35.499 --> 00:01:39.012
But all 16 of those members aren't
doing the same job they were doing 12

00:01:39.012 --> 00:01:39.641
months ago.

00:01:39.641 --> 00:01:42.947
Each and everyone of them is
doing something more, acting

00:01:42.947 --> 00:01:47.941
at an elevated position, or even taking on
additional roles and responsibilities that

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:52.200
are setting them for their next kind
of professional step or development.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.795
Brand and
taste come before everything else.

00:01:54.795 --> 00:01:59.715
Taste has to absolutely be there, but
the brand has to pop enough at the shelf.

00:01:59.715 --> 00:02:03.015
What you have to do really closely is
listen to what the consumer wants,

00:02:03.015 --> 00:02:04.505
because the consumer has the power.

00:02:04.505 --> 00:02:09.486
And the consumer will be sure with their
dollars to vote one way or another,

00:02:09.486 --> 00:02:11.950
but they'll signal what they want.

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:15.429
So what lured me to Beanfields
specifically was just the fact that it

00:02:15.429 --> 00:02:19.580
was on a downward trajectory, that they
had already taken a couple of swings at it

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:22.650
with other leaders and
that it quite hadn't gotten there.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.082
So it's like, yeah,
let me let me try that,

00:02:25.082 --> 00:02:27.392
see if that seems like a worthy challenge.

00:02:27.392 --> 00:02:32.327
And wait, there's also these other
aspects to it, the B Corporation aspect,

00:02:32.327 --> 00:02:35.348
the partnership with
farmers in North Dakota and

00:02:35.348 --> 00:02:38.897
continue to promote conventional and
organic farming.

00:02:38.897 --> 00:02:43.150
Now on the social impact side, the fact
that we get to partner with a nonprofit,

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:44.357
Homeboy Industries,

00:02:44.357 --> 00:02:48.370
that's helping to rehabilitate
previously incarcerated gang members.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:51.342
When you weave in all those pieces, it
certainly makes working here fulfilling.

00:02:51.342 --> 00:02:56.164
But I think those are key components
that most brands are aspiring

00:02:56.164 --> 00:03:00.472
to include today in developing a food and
beverage brand.

00:03:00.472 --> 00:03:04.368
So it's been some time since
I graduated from the GSB.

00:03:04.368 --> 00:03:08.285
Fast-forwarding to today and
what matters to me most hasn't changed.

00:03:08.285 --> 00:03:12.674
I think the tools and the experiences that
I picked up by the GBS help keep it in

00:03:12.674 --> 00:03:16.115
perspective for me, and
they're certainly hard skills.

00:03:16.115 --> 00:03:18.821
I think the one that
probably serves me the most,

00:03:18.821 --> 00:03:21.069
certainly inter- personal dynamics.

00:03:21.069 --> 00:03:23.428
The business part of businesses easy,

00:03:23.428 --> 00:03:26.650
it's the people part that's
always the challenge.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:31.249
Three core things that are coming to

00:03:31.249 --> 00:03:36.307
mind that stick with me until this day,

00:03:36.307 --> 00:03:39.987
it's how you treat people,

00:03:39.987 --> 00:03:45.829
hard work ethic and
take pride in your craft.

00:03:45.829 --> 00:03:47.306
[MUSIC]

